# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# Node (for any tooling layered on top)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo

# Build artifacts that DO NOT belong in version control
# (Phase 1+ may generate these; tracked separately by run manifests)
# Contents of data/raw/ are excluded, but the DIRECTORY is not — git cannot
# re-include a path from inside an excluded directory, and two artifacts below
# must stay tracked (see the exceptions further down).
data/raw/*
data/runs/*/raw/
data/evidence/*.pdf

# Per-county run logs and transient artifacts
# The runs/<slug>/ folder itself IS committed (launch files, manifests, notes).
# But per-county logs are scratch and not committed.
runs/*/logs/
runs/*/tmp/
runs/*/.cache/

# §01.22 sample-document pulls. Recon MUST fetch and inspect real source
# documents; it MUST NOT commit them. These are raw records carrying real owner
# names, situs addresses and party names — same class as data/raw/. The recon
# report cites their paths and findings; the files stay local.
runs/*/recon/samples/

# dashboard/index.html IS published — it is the GitHub Pages artifact, served
# publicly at https://xcerebroai.github.io/marion-county-intel/ , mirroring how
# harris-intel publishes dashboard/index.html + records.json. It embeds the full
# unredacted record set by operator decision. Regenerate with:
#   .venv\Scripts\python.exe scrapers\build_dashboard.py

# Exceptions to data/raw/ — these two are committed on purpose.
#   run_logs/   per-run counts only (rows, new instruments, capped slices). No
#               owner names, no addresses. Committed so a silent-zero
#               regression is visible in history rather than invisible.
#   first_seen.json  the newness ledger: source|instrument -> first capture
#               date. Instrument numbers are document identifiers, not people.
#               Must persist across CI runs or every record looks new forever.
!data/raw/run_logs/
!data/raw/run_logs/**
!data/raw/first_seen.json

# NOTE: every Marion adapter artifact is written under data/raw/ — the crosswalk
# (data/raw/crosswalk/), the review queue, and the run report included. They all
# carry real owner names and situs addresses, so they are covered by the
# data/raw/ rule above and are additionally skipped by the framework PII guard,
# which excludes any path containing a "raw" component. Do not relocate them out
# of data/raw/: doing so both leaks PII into history and makes the gate scan
# ~150 MB of owner names (it times out, then fails).

# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key

# Coverage / test artifacts
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/
